<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Sultanate of Oman</h1><p class="st-meta">1970 CE – present · capital Muscat</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Modern Oman under Sultan Qaboos and his successor, transformed since 1970 from isolation into a stable, neutral Gulf state.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 23 July 1970 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qaboos-bin-said">Qaboos bin Said</a> deposed his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/said-bin-taimur">Said bin Taimur</a>, ending the isolation of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-muscat-and-oman">Sultanate of Muscat and Oman</a>, and renamed the country the Sultanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a>. He invited exiles home and launched a programme of roads, schools and hospitals funded by oil.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qaboos-bin-said">Qaboos</a> ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhofar">Dhofar</a> rebellion by 1975 with British, Iranian and Jordanian help and with development aid to the south. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> is an absolute monarchy; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basic-statute-of-oman">Basic Statute</a> of 1996 codified the system, and an elected consultative council has limited powers. The country's Ibadi tradition, foreign policy of neutrality and role as mediator, including between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a>, set it apart in the region.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qaboos-bin-said">Qaboos</a> died in January 2020 after nearly fifty years in power. His cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haitham-bin-tariq">Haitham bin Tariq</a> succeeded him and introduced fiscal reforms and a named crown prince.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate, 1970 CE – present"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">sultanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Arabia and the Gulf</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:98.91%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1970 CE – present</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Muscat</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Qaboos bin Said, Haitham bin Tariq</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ibadi Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Oman</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Oman</dd></dl></aside></div>
